@page "/our-history"

<SeoHead Title="Our History - CACI"
         Description="The journey of CACI from 2002 to present. Apostolic Roots, Growth, and Succession."
         CanonicalUrl="https://caci.life/our-history" />

<section class="section-padding timeline-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
            <h1>Our Story: Apostolic Roots & Growth</h1>
            <div class="divider"></div>
            <p>The journey of Covenant Apostolic Congregations Intl.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline">
            <div class="timeline-container left">
                <div class="timeline-content">
                    <h2>2002: Pre-Formation</h2>
                    <p>Key ministers gathered in Mobile, AL, instrumental in the doctrinal formulation of what would
                        become CACI. The meeting brought together the 7th Day understanding, Apostolic Structure,
                        and the Coming Kingdom message.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-container right">
                <div class="timeline-content">
                    <h2>2003: The Official Start</h2>
                    <p>The first official CACI convention was held in Mobile, AL. The network grew over the next few
                        years to reach multiple States in the USA, as well as Australia, the Caribbean, and the
                        Philippines.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-container left">
                <div class="timeline-content">
                    <h2>2011: The Festival Shake-up</h2>
                    <p>Leading Bishops began to recognize their early position opposing the Scriptural Festivals was
                        incorrect. This created a shake-up as some congregations kept to a Non-Festival position
                        while others embraced the new-found experience.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-container right">
                <div class="timeline-content">
                    <h2>2014: Doctrinal Settlement and Growth</h2>
                    <p>The issue was settled, and CACI became Apostolic in Doctrine, Sacraments, the Celebration of
                        the Feasts and Sabbaths, and the heralding of the Coming Kingdom. The Feasts set the stage
                        for exponential growth.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-container left">
                <div class="timeline-content">
                    <h2>2016: Apostolic Council & Succession</h2>
                    <p>Presiding Bishop Jesse White formed the CACI Council of Apostolic Bishops, passing Apostolic
                        Succession by Consecrating and Establishing Apostolic Agreement with each member of the
                        Council.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-footer">
            <div class="timeline-content">
                <h2>Apostolic Succession</h2>
                <p>Though the CACI does not consider "Apostolic Succession" to be necessary to biblical doctrine and
                    faith, we do possess proof of our historic lineage back to the time of the first Apostles.</p>
                <ul class="styled-list">
                    <li><strong>All CACI Bishops Are Consecrated "IN" Apostolic
                            Succession</strong><br><small>(Bishops may pass this Episcopal Succession only with a
                            valid and current Apostolic Agreement)</small></li>
                    <li><strong>All CACI Elders & Ministers Are Ordained & Appointed "UNDER" Apostolic
                            Succession</strong><br><small>(Thus Elders are duly Authorized & Ordained to perform
                            their Holy Order)<br>(Ministers are duly Appointed & Sent to aid in the Gospel
                            work)</small></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
